{
  "text": "```verilog\nmodule pulse_sync #(\n    parameter STAGES = 2\n)(\n    input  clk_a,\n    input  rstn_a,\n    input  clk_b,\n    input  rstn_b,\n    input  pulseA_i,\n    output pulseB_o,\n    output busy_o\n);\n\n    // Domain A: Toggle a bit on each accepted pulse\n    reg a_toggle;\n    wire a_toggle_next;\n\n    // Domain B: Synchronize the toggle bit\n    reg [STAGES-1:0] b_sync;\n    reg b_toggle_prev;\n\n    // Generate pulse in domain B from toggle change\n    wire b_toggle_change;\n    assign b_toggle_change = b_sync[STAGES-1] ^ b_toggle_prev;\n\n    assign pulseB_o = b_toggle_change;\n    assign busy_o   = b_sync[STAGES-1];\n\n    // Domain A logic\n    // Accept pulse only when not busy (i.e., when the toggle has been acknowledged)\n    // We use the synchronized toggle value fed back? No, that would be a data path.\n    // Instead, we use a handshake: Domain A sets a \"pending\" flag, Domain B clears it.\n    // But the requirement says \"one-pulse-in, one-pulse-out\" with busy_o.\n    // A simpler approach: Use a toggle bit. Domain A toggles on pulse.\n    // Domain B detects the toggle change and outputs a pulse.\n    // busy_o is high while the toggle is \"in flight\" - but how does Domain A know?\n    // Actually, for a simple pulse synchronizer with toggle, busy_o can be derived\n    // from the synchronized toggle in Domain B, but that's in Domain B.\n    // The busy_o output is in Domain B (since it's an output port, and pulseB_o is in Domain B).\n    // Wait, busy_o is an output. It should be in Domain B since it relates to the pulse being in flight.\n    // But the requirement says \"ignore additional pulseA_i while busy\". This means Domain A needs to know busy state.\n    // So we need a feedback path from Domain B to Domain A for the busy signal.\n    // This is a 2-phase handshake.\n\n    // Let's use a proper 2-phase handshake:\n    // Domain A: req (request)\n    // Domain B: ack (acknowledge)\n    // Pulse in A: set req\n    // Pulse in B: detect req change, output pulse, set ack\n    // Domain A: detect ack change, clear req\n    // busy_o: req is high (pulse in flight)\n\n    // Actually, let's reconsider. The simplest safe approach for \"one pulse in, one pulse out\"\n    // with busy is a toggle-based synchronizer where busy is derived from the toggle state.\n    // But busy needs to be visible to Domain A to gate input pulses.\n\n    // Let's use a 2-phase handshake with proper CDC:\n    // - req: Domain A -> Domain B (synchronized)\n    // - ack: Domain B -> Domain A (synchronized)\n\n    reg req;\n    reg ack;\n\n    // Synchronize req to Domain B\n    reg [STAGES-1:0] req_sync;\n    always @(posedge clk_b or negedge rstn_b) begin\n        if (!rstn_b)\n            req_sync <= {STAGES{1'b0}};\n        else\n            req_sync <= {req_sync[STAGES-2:0], req};\n    end\n\n    // Synchronize ack to Domain A\n    reg [STAGES-1:0] ack_sync;\n    always @(posedge clk_a or negedge rstn_a) begin\n        if (!rstn_a)\n            ack_sync <= {STAGES{1'b0}};\n        else\n            ack_sync <= {ack_sync[STAGES-2:0], ack};\n    end\n\n    // Domain B: Detect req change, generate pulse, toggle ack\n    reg req_prev;\n    wire req_change;\n    assign req_change = req_sync[STAGES-1] ^ req_prev;\n\n    always @(posedge clk_b or negedge rstn_b) begin\n        if (!rstn_b) begin\n            req_prev <= 1'b0;\n            ack <= 1'b0;\n        end else begin\n            req_prev <= req_sync[STAGES-1];\n            if (req_change)\n                ack <= ~ack;\n        end\n    end\n\n    assign pulseB_o = req_change;\n\n    // Domain A: Accept pulse, set req, wait for ack change, clear req\n    reg ack_prev;\n    wire ack_change;\n    assign ack_change = ack_sync[STAGES-1] ^ ack_prev;\n\n    always @(posedge clk_a or negedge rstn_a) begin\n        if (!rstn_a) begin\n            req <= 1'b0;\n            ack_prev <= 1'b0;\n        end else begin\n            ack_prev <= ack_sync[STAGES-1];\n            if (ack_change)\n                req <= 1'b0;\n            else if (pulseA_i && !req)\n                req <= 1'b1;\n        end\n    end\n\n    assign busy_o = req;\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
